    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by **Jose Caballero**, who registers our highest efficiency score of 80.26. His matchup against the southpaw Lopez provides a critical +13% platoon boost, and when paired with an advantageous park environment and a secure #5 spot in the order, he represents our premier play for stabilizing our stolen base targets. **Corbin Carroll** (73.68) and **Brice Turang** (71.97) follow closely behind; while **Corbin Carroll** faces a formidable matchup against Miller, his elite sprint speed and elevated xwOBA of 0.373 make him an auto-start, while **Brice Turang** benefits from a high-leverage SP matchup against Imai (5.17 xERA), allowing him to maximize his efficiency on the basepaths.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 51.66 score. While his raw talent is significant, he is currently suppressed by a difficult matchup against Lodolo (3.83 xERA) and the reality that he offers zero support in our high-priority stolen base category. This forced the inclusion of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, who, despite lower base projections, occupy vital slots in our daily capacity management. We are also monitoring **Seiya Suzuki** closely; his 59.21 score is contingent on his presumed #6 spot in the lineup. Should the official release bump him down the order or expose him to defensive substitution risks, we remain ready to pivot to safer bench depth, though we remain optimistic given his historical proficiency against left-handed pitching. **Mickey Moniak** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving the rest of the bench\u2014including **Zach McKinstry**, **Travis Bazzana**, and the injured **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014to await further opportunities as we navigate this stretch of the season.",
